&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trust &amp;amp; Safety Experience owns the customer journeys during authentication, verification, and fraud journeys. You will work as a Frontend engineer, contributing to web, and mobile interfaces. In this role, you will need to gain a deep understanding of the business, product and engineering context, and utilize that context to own and deliver high-availability and low-latency systems that Affirm customers use every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;· You will be responsible for owning and delivering quarterly goals for your team, leading engineers on your team through ambiguity to solve open-ended problems, and ensuring that everyone is supported throughout delivery.&lt;br&gt;· You will support your peers and stakeholders in the product development lifecycle by collaborating with product management, design &amp;amp; analytics by participating in ideation, articulating technical constraints, and partnering on decisions that properly consider risks and trade-offs.&lt;br&gt;· You will proactively identify project, process, technology or business issues, advocate for them, and lead in solving them.&lt;br&gt;· You will support the operations and availability of your team’s artifacts by creating and monitoring metrics, escalating when needed, and supporting “keep the lights on” &amp;amp; on-call efforts.&lt;br&gt;· You will foster a culture of quality and ownership on your team by setting or improving code review and design standards for your team, and advocating for them beyond your team through your writing and tech talks.&lt;br&gt;· You will help develop talent on your team by providing feedback and guidance, and leading by example.&lt;br&gt;. This position requires either equivalent practical experience or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;· You have 4+ years of experience of developing and architecting web applications using declarative UI frameworks like React or Vue.&lt;br&gt;· You are proficient in working with &lt;span class=&quot;WGK0&quot;&gt;Javascript/Typescript.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;· You have experience defining a technical plan for the delivery of a significant feature or system component with an elegant, simple and extensible design. You write high quality code that is easily understood and used by others.&lt;br&gt;· You are proficient at making significant changes in a large code base, and have developed a suite of tools and practices that enable you and your team to do so safely.&lt;br&gt;· Your experience demonstrates that you take ownership of your growth, proactively seeking feedback from your team, your manager, and your stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;· You have strong verbal and written communication skills that support effective collaboration with our global engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires either equivalent practical experience or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Grade - N&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grade - 9&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: 195,000 - 255,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: 173,000 - 233,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Revenue team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue team drives Affirm’s top-line growth through strategic partnerships, pricing, and go-to-market execution. We acquire, retain, and expand merchant relationships across eCommerce, in-store, telesales, and the Affirm app. The team leads onboarding, relationship management, and performance optimization to help partners succeed. We deliver value-added solutions, drive adoption, and support long-term business growth by connecting merchants and consumers through Affirm’s products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for intelligent, driven professionals to join our Revenue Analytics team. This team is responsible for comprehensive analyses, reporting, and data solutions to support and grow our Revenue segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have strong analytical and problem solving skills, the ability to craft comprehensive narratives for both internal and external stakeholders, and produce tools and solutions to scale data usage with Revenue. In addition to analytical rigor, the ideal candidate has strong interpersonal skills to work proactively within the organization and with clients to drive forward recommendations. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize decisions and execution with analyses, and communicate to internal and external partners&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be a strategic partner with our Client Success and Marketplace Teams as the data SME for respective Revenue segments and merchants for their point-of-sale and Marketplace business&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create business cases, insights, and dashboards as well as handle experiments to engage Affirm’s external merchant base; demonstrating Affirm’s value proposition and product performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create internal analyses to assess Revenue performance, drive recommendations, and inform critical decisions; using insights to serve segment strategy and execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Standardize common use cases, provide the analytics infrastructure, and automate analyses and dashboards to scale decisions and execution within Revenue and with top external merchants&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own comprehensive analytics solution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define KPIs, performance benchmarks, and methodologies, including identifying and working with unstructured and structured data sources (in-house and third-party) to enable solutions and generate actionable insights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide project and analytics guidance to a cross-functional team, acting as the analytics point of contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Propose, monitor, and contextualize experiment design and execution to drive optimizations of Affirm’s GTM efforts, empirically quantify the value of Affirm to our prospective merchants, and upsell enhanced offers to existing merchants&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of experience in an analytically-driven role (consulting, finance, analytics, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong working knowledge of SQL, data visualization tools (e.g. Sigma, Looker, Tableau). Understanding or a demonstrated aptitude to learn Python is a plus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated aptitude in leveraging AI tools for analytics (Cursor, Claude Code, etc.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional problem-solving skills, including ability to operate in ambiguity and establishing analytical frameworks to apply to business problems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to create structure in ambiguous situations, such as aligning stakeholders, or choosing the most impactful data to drive decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to communicate effectively, and craft compelling narratives to influence business and technical stakeholders across all levels of the organization, internally and externally&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong organization and execution skills, including ability to operate independently and drive multiple strategic initiatives simultaneously to drive business goals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior track record in building successful cross-functional relationships with partners internally and externally&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Self-starter and a track record of successfully driving projects from end to end (from building strategy to implementation)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Passion and drive to disrupt both the retail and lending industry for the better&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enough laziness to find a faster way to do your least favorite tasks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Humility and a team player - you go out of your way to help teammates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of the FinTech or Payments industry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience performing data analytics for marketplace platforms&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated aptitude in AI tools for analytics (Cursor, Claude Code, etc.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
